Operational reports summarize the performance, health, and management of Azure environments over a defined period. These reports help technical teams and management evaluate service quality and identify trends.

Typical report sections include:

* Availability statistics
* Incident summaries
* Performance metrics
* Backup status
* Security findings
* Cost analysis
* Capacity utilization
* Improvement recommendations

For example, monthly reports may show recurring storage performance issues that justify infrastructure improvements.

A real-life use case is IT leadership reviewing cloud operations during management meetings.

Regular reporting supports informed decision-making and continuous improvement.
